From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ios-blink-sideload <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:09:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS sideload: use the system fonts for system-ui and friends

Blink's iOS port had no mapping for the system font: system-ui fell back
to Times, and BlinkMacSystemFont / -apple-system / ui-monospace, which most
sites use, were unknown families. Pages therefore never used SF Pro or SF
Mono.

- font_cache.cc: on iOS, as on Mac, create and cache system-ui like any
  other family instead of diverting it to SystemFontPlatformData(), which
  had no family to use.
- font_cache_skia.cc / ios/font_cache_ios.mm: build system-ui and
  ui-sans-serif, ui-serif, ui-monospace and ui-rounded from UIKit's system
  font designs (SF Pro, New York, SF Mono, SF Rounded; CoreText's
  fixed-pitch UI font is Menlo), with the requested weight and slant, and
  set the 'opsz' axis to the text size as the Mac port does. Without it
  HarfBuzz shapes with the default instance and body text is about 7%
  tighter than in Safari.
- style_builder_converter.cc: treat -apple-system and BlinkMacSystemFont
  as system-ui, as Safari on iOS does.

Status: verified at Chromium 4558926c in the iOS 27 simulator (iPhone 13
mini): system-ui, -apple-system and BlinkMacSystemFont render in SF Pro
and ui-monospace in SF Mono, with spacing within 1% of Safari.

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/css/resolver/style_builder_converter.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/css/resolver/style_builder_converter.cc
index 867c60e8fc76df10b556ba334746ea0e348750ea..f914efb410d9a7dc56df5bbe39457200f3f24ef0 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/css/resolver/style_builder_converter.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/css/resolver/style_builder_converter.cc
@@ -563,6 +563,14 @@ FontDescription::FamilyDescription StyleBuilderConverterBase::ConvertFontFamily(
       // If system-ui comes before BlinkMacSystemFont don't use-count.
       count_blink_mac_system_font = false;
     }
+#elif BUILDFLAG(IS_IOS)
+    // [ios-blink-sideload] Like Safari on iOS, and BlinkMacSystemFont on Mac,
+    // -apple-system and BlinkMacSystemFont name the system font.
+    if (IsA<CSSFontFamilyValue>(*family) &&
+        (family_name == font_family_names::kBlinkMacSystemFont ||
+         EqualIgnoringAsciiCase(family_name, "-apple-system"))) {
+      family_name = font_family_names::kSystemUi;
+    }
 #endif
 
     if (desc.generic_family == FontDescription::GenericFamilyType::kNoFamily) {
diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/BUILD.gn b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/BUILD.gn
index 5f0673a7eed61cf15d645bf6b8b4f2260f1d0a39..9f3a6a29d286984297d8cf4dc976035d2768f908 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/BUILD.gn
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/BUILD.gn
@@ -1781,7 +1781,13 @@ component("platform") {
